  "id": "cataphasia",
  "term": "cataphasia",
  "definition": "Cataphasia is a historical term for a severe deterioration of speech, usually associated with serious nervous disease, in which a person repeatedly says the same word or phrase. It was also used for markedly reduced sentence formation, with childlike, minimally grammatical speech and frequent repetition.",
